          "text": "{\n  \"occurrence_id\": \"bronte-jane-eyre-f221719b1af4\",\n  \"label_support\": {\n    \"truth_conditional\": 4,\n    \"performative\": 1,\n    \"exclamatory_reflexive\": 0\n  },\n  \"construals\": [\n    {\n      \"perspective\": \"speaker\",\n      \"analysis\": \"The putative speaker is represented as avowing an existing love while deliberately withholding an offer or commitment: his heart is already dedicated elsewhere, and that fact 'keeps me dumb.' The words are narratively supplied as the content of his look rather than actually spoken.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"perspective\": \"hearer\",\n      \"analysis\": \"She appears aware of his emotional susceptibility—'she knew her power'—but the passage does not establish that she construes his look as conveying every proposition in the quoted passage.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"perspective\": \"narrator_or_text\",\n      \"analysis\": \"The text interprets trembling, a burning eye, and a 'sad and resolute look' as if they expressed a detailed avowal of love, confidence of reciprocation, and refusal to pursue the relationship.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"perspective\": \"reader\",\n      \"analysis\": \"A reader is strongly invited to accept love as the emotional state behind his visible reactions, while recognizing that the quoted wording is an inferred rendering of nonverbal behavior rather than a literal utterance.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"features\": [\n    \"quoted\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"text\": \"his hand would tremble and his eye burn\",\n      \"supports\": \"Bodily signs provide textual grounds for the narrator's attribution of intense emotion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"He seemed to say, with his sad and resolute look\",\n      \"supports\": \"The quotation represents an interpretation of nonverbal expression, not words established as actually spoken.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"if he did not say it with his lips\",\n      \"supports\": \"The text explicitly distinguishes the attributed message from a literal verbal declaration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"I love you\",\n      \"supports\": \"In the represented content, this directly avows a current loving state and therefore strongly supports the truth-conditional reading.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"It is not despair of success that keeps me dumb\",\n      \"supports\": \"His silence is presented as deliberate restraint, weakening any reading of the words as an actual undertaking.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"If I offered my heart, I believe you would accept it\",\n      \"supports\": \"The offer is counterfactual rather than enacted; this gives only weak support to a performative reading.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"that heart is already laid on a sacred altar\",\n      \"supports\": \"An existing prior dedication prevents the avowal from functioning as a new romantic commitment.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"needs_more_context\": true,\n  \"context_request\": \"Further context could show whether she consciously interprets his look as an avowal, whether he intends his feelings to be communicated, and how reliable or figurative the narrator's detailed rendering of the look is.\",\n  \"typology_adequate\": true,\n  \"typology_diagnosis\": \"The truth-conditional category naturally describes the content attributed to the man: he loves her. Performative force is weak because he remains silent and explicitly frames offering his heart as counterfactual. The production is too coherent and propositionally elaborate to be primarily exclamatory/reflexive. The chief complication is orthogonal to T/P/E: the declaration is narratively imputed to a look rather than literally uttered.\",\n  \"proposed_missing_dimensions\": [\n    \"Actual utterance versus narratively supplied verbalization of nonverbal behavior\",\n    \"Intended communication versus an observer's inference from involuntary signs\"\n  ],\n  \"confidence\": 0.95\n}"
